---
/**
 * Root layout. Every route renders through this.
 *
 * The direction contract below MUST remain the first child of <body> and
 * MUST survive the production build — it is the auditable record of the
 * visual world every component inherits. Do not move it into a child or
 * slotted component; Astro strips a slot's leading comment.
 */
interface Props {
  title: string;
  description: string;
}

const { title, description } = Astro.props;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <!--
    THESIS: Six shipped projects presented as consigned goods with placards,
    each carrying its own lot code, consignee and stamped status. Refuses the
    dark developer-portfolio card grid and its cream-editorial opposite alike.

    OWN-WORLD: Kraft/manila board ground, black stencil ink, one safety accent.
    Condensed grotesque caps; monospace reserved for real codes only. Hazard-band
    rules, rubber-stamped status marks, lot numbers, consignee lines. One label
    stock across all 11 routes; a single vertical registration axis everything
    aligns to; density itself is tone, never decoration.

    STORY: A founder understands this person ships real things, believes five of
    six are genuinely live, and opens a case study.

    FIRST VIEWPORT: Consignment placard top-left — GARY REYES, INDUSTRIAL
    ENGINEERING, DLSU, MANILA — set as a shipping mark against the registration
    axis, lot/date stamp opposite. Work begins immediately below as placarded
    units. Primary action: the first unit.

    FORM: Shipping manifest / logistics labeling; candidate 3 of 7; seed d4e5136b.

    FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the
    finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
    -->
    <slot />
  </body>
</html>
